From 40f1b36c642e7e5ea552b82976a2e5e31a0313d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonas Heinle <jonasheinle@googlemail.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 21:07:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] [AArch64] Report SEH pseudos as zero-size

The SEH_* pseudos only emit unwind opcodes into .xdata, never a code
byte. They are not meta-instructions, so getInstSizeInBytes fell through
to the default case and reported each one as a normal 4-byte
instruction. A prologue emits one per saved register, so on Windows
every function's size estimate was inflated.

This one is conservative, not a miscompile: BranchRelaxation relaxes
branches it does not need to, and AArch64CompressJumpTables leaves jump
tables wider than they have to be.

Size = 0 in AArch64InstrInfo.td cannot express this. The default case
tests `if (Desc.getSize())`, so a declared zero reads as "unset" and
still gives 4. I tried that first and measured no change at all.

Assisted-by: Claude (Anthropic)
---
 llvm/lib/Target/AArch64/AArch64InstrInfo.cpp | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/llvm/lib/Target/AArch64/AArch64InstrInfo.cpp b/llvm/lib/Target/AArch64/AArch64InstrInfo.cpp
index 43aab1400e81..673ee8bd5949 100644
--- a/llvm/lib/Target/AArch64/AArch64InstrInfo.cpp
+++ b/llvm/lib/Target/AArch64/AArch64InstrInfo.cpp
@@ -220,6 +220,11 @@ unsigned AArch64InstrInfo::getInstSizeInBytes(const MachineInstr &MI) const {
   if (MI.isMetaInstruction())
     return 0;
 
+  // SEH pseudos only emit unwind opcodes into .xdata. Size = 0 in the .td does
+  // not work: the default case below treats getSize() == 0 as "unset".
+  if (isSEHInstruction(MI))
+    return 0;
+
   // FIXME: We currently only handle pseudoinstructions that don't get expanded
   //        before the assembly printer.
   unsigned NumBytes = 0;
-- 
2.55.0.windows.3

